}

.slide{
  .id{mise-machine}
  .title{A Machine, Not an Endpoint}
  .body{
    .h1{A Machine, Not an Endpoint}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chell}
      .o{.typewriter{chris@cube:...loads$ cd ~/uploads/SAG-anon}}
      .o{.typewriter{chris@cube:...-anon$ ls /bin | head -3
 adc-to-zmap-nii-scale-up-v0.1.0
 adc-to-zmap-nii-scale-up-v0.2.1
 adc-to-zmap-nii-scale-up-v0.2.2}}
      .o{.typewriter{chris@cube:...-anon$ whatif pl-fshack-v1.5.0 --inputFile brain.mgz
  on   a new feed, rooted by pl-dircopy of /home/chris/uploads/SAG-anon
whatif: pl-fshack-v1.5.0 was not run; nothing was created}}
      .o{.typewriter{chris@cube:...-anon$ cat /proc/jobs/feed_123/pl-dircopy_788/pl-fshack_789/status
finishedSuccessfully}}
    }
    .takeaway{DATA IS A FILESYSTEM. A PLUGIN IS A COMMAND. A JOB IS A FILE.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-layers}
  .title{Above CUBE}
  .body{
    .h1{Above CUBE}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> mise --layers}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
             ┌─────────────┬──────────────┐
             │    <b>chell</b>    │    <b>argus</b>     │   <i><b>how you look</b>: a terminal, a browser</i>
       ┌─────┴─────────────┴──────────────┤
       │             <b>calypso</b>              │   <i><b>who is there</b>: one login, one live session</i>
 ┌─────┴──────────────────────────────────┤
 │                  <b>mise</b>                  │   <i><b>where things are</b>: /home  /bin  /proc</i>
 ├────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │                  <b>CUBE</b>                  │   <i><b>what is true</b>: the objects and their laws</i>
 └────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{Below CUBE, swap the .bf{cluster}.}
      .o{Above CUBE, swap the .bf{surface}.}
    }
    .takeaway{CUBE SAYS WHAT IS TRUE. mise SAYS WHERE THINGS ARE.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-stack}
  .title{The Whole Stack}
  .body{
    .h1{The Whole Stack}
    .h2{Three machines, two networks}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> mise --stack}
<pre class="fig wide">
 ┌─ <b>your machine</b> ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   <i>a terminal, a browser,</i>
 │ ┌──────────┐                           you                                       │   <i>and programs of your own</i>
 │ │ a program│                            │                                        │
 │ └─┬────────┘                   ┌────────┴────────┐                               │
 │   ┆ ┌──────────┐               │                 │                               │
 │   ┆ │ a program│         ┌─────┴─────┐     ┌─────┴─────┐                         │
 │   ┆ └─┬────────┘         │   <b>chell</b>   │     │   <b>ARGUS</b>   │                         │   <i>surfaces: two views of one session</i>
 │   ┆   ┆ ┌──────────┐     │ terminal  │     │  browser  │                         │
 │   ┆   ┆ │ a program│     └─────┬─────┘     └─────┬─────┘                         │
 │   ┆   ┆ └─┬────────┘        ws │                 │ https, then ws                <i>│</i>
 │   ┆   ┆   ┆                    └────────┬────────┘                               │
 │   ┆   ┆   ┆                             └───┐                                    │
 └───┼───┼───┼─────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┘
     ┆   ┆   ┆                                 │  menu: the wire, across a network
 ╔═══╪═══╪═══╪═════════════════════════════════╪══ <b>the bastion</b> ═════════════════════╗   <i>one Linux host: VM, container or metal</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆                                 │                                    ║
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆                     ┌───────────┴───────────┐                        ║
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆                     │         <b>porter</b>        │                        ║   <i>the login page (gdm)</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆                     ├───────────────────────┤    ┌───────────────┐   <i>║   the console's own terminal, on a pty</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆                     │        <b>calypso</b>        ├──┬─┤  <b>chell (pty)</b>  │   <i>║   your session, long-lived (tmux + sshd)</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆               ┌─────┴───────────────────────┤  │ └───────────────┘   <i>║</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   ┆               │                             │  │                     <i>║</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆   └┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┤            <b>brasa</b>            │  │ ┌───────────────┐   <i>║   the shell engine (bash + coreutils)</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆                   │                             │  └─┤    <i>the host   │   ║</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆             ┌─────┴─────────────────────────────┤    │ a shell       <i>│   ║   reached by `!`, under host control</i>
 ║   ┆   ┆             │                                   │    │ ~/project     <i>│   ║   the dev environment: edit, build, run</i>
 ║   ┆   └┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┤                <b>fond</b>               │    └───────────────┘   <i>║   the filesystem interface (the VFS)</i>
 ║   ┆                 │                                   │                        ║
 ║   ┆           ┌─────┴───────────────────────────────────┤                        ║
 ║   ┆           │                                         │                        ║
 ║   └┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┤               <b>chris driver</b>              │                        ║   <i>a filesystem driver: CUBE as a tree</i>
 ║               │   salsa   the tree, and its logic       │                        ║
 ║               │   cumin   CUBE's REST, via chrisapi     │                        ║
 ║               └─────────────────────────────┬───────────┘                        ║
 ║                                             │                                    ║
 ╚═════════════════════════════════════════════╪════════════════════════════════════╝
                                               │  HTTPS, Collection+JSON, across a network
                                    ┌─────────────────────┐
                                   ╱                     ╱│
                                  ╱         <b>CUBE</b>        ╱ │
                                 ╱                     ╱  │
                                ┌─────────────────────┐   │
                                │                     │   │                            ChRIS: users, data, plugins, compute,
                                │                     │   ┘                            and the record of every run
                                │       what is       │  ╱
                                │         true        │ ╱
                                │                     │╱
                                └─────────────────────┘
 
 <b>────</b><i>  a call, over a network</i>
 <b>┄┄┄┄</b><i>  the same package, linked into a program of your own: its own engine, its own process</i>
</pre>
    }
    .takeaway{CUBE IS THE ONLY SOURCE OF TRUTH. EVERYTHING ABOVE IT IS A VIEW OF IT.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise, README}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-kernel}
  .title{The Intent Kernel}
  .body{
    .h1{The Intent Kernel}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> brasa --contract}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 ┌───────┐   ─── <b>intent</b> ────<u>▶</u>   ┌─────────┐   ─── <i>validated actions</i> ───<u>▶</u>    ┌────────┐
 │  you  │                      │  <b>brasa</b>  │                                 │  <b>CUBE</b>  │
 └───────┘   <u>◀</u>── <b>receipt</b> ────   └─────────┘   <u>◀</u>── <i>what really happened</i> ──   └────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{Say .bf{what} you want, not how.}
      .o{A .bf{bounded} vocabulary. No arbitrary API calls.}
      .o{The engine writes the .bf{receipt}, not the caller.}
      .o{No loops, no .bf{if}. Those stay in your script.}
    }
    .takeaway{NO SURFACE TOUCHES THE RAW API.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise · docs/intent-kernel.adoc}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-intent}
  .title{One Intent, Four Ways}
  .body{
    .h1{One Intent, Four Ways}
    .h2{List one directory under your uploads}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> ls ~/uploads/SAG-anon --from=everywhere}
    .nexus{.id{intent-ways}
      .div{.jump{.target{intent-shell} From the Shell}}
      .div{.jump{.target{intent-program} From a Program}}
      .div{.jump{.target{intent-wire} Over the Wire}}
      .div{.jump{.target{intent-raw} Without mise}}
    }
    }
    .source{harbor-medical-ai.github.io/mise}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{intent-shell}
  .title{From the Shell}
  .body{
    .h1{From the Shell}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chell}
      .o{.typewriter{chris@cube:...loads$ ls -l ~/uploads/SAG-anon
@DIR1  d chris   0        2026-10-16 13:35:18  00005-Synthesized_T1-abcdef0/
@FIL1  - chris   320      2026-10-16 13:35:46  sphere.nii.gz
numbered: @DIR1, @FIL1}}
      .o{One .bf{line}.}
      .o{Handles like .bf{@FIL1} feed the next command.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE COMMAND IS THE INTENT.}
    .source{chell 5.20.7, captured live · harbor-medical-ai.github.io/mise/guide-chell.html}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{intent-program}
  .title{From a Program}
  .body{
    .h1{From a Program}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> cat list.ts}
      .o{
.code{.syntax{language=typescript}
import { chellApi_create, type ChellApi, type TypedEnvelope } from '@fnndsc/brasa';
import type { ListingItem } from '@fnndsc/menu';
/**
 * List the entry names of one ChRIS directory.
 * @param path - Directory to list, as chell would address it.
 * @returns The entry names; empty if the listing failed.
 */
async function directoryNames_list(path: string): Promise<string[]> {
  const sh: ChellApi = await chellApi_create();
  const listing: TypedEnvelope<'fs.listing'> = await sh.ls(path);
  const items: ListingItem[] = listing.model?.data[0]?.items ?? [];
  if (listing.status !== 'ok') return [];
  return items.map((item: ListingItem): string => item.name);
}
}
}
    }
    .takeaway{THE SAME COMMAND, AS A FUNCTION CALL. SHIPPED, IN-PROCESS, ON NODE.}
    .source{typechecked against mise main, not run; assumes a connection made with chrisConnection_init · mise/guide-chell.html}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{intent-wire}
  .title{Over the Wire}
  .body{
    .h1{Over the Wire}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> wscat --connect calypso}
      .o{
.code{.syntax{language=json}
{"type": "execute", "id": "1", "line": "ls /home/chris/uploads/SAG-anon"}
}
}
      .o{
.code{.syntax{language=json}
{"type": "result", "id": "1", "envelopes": [{"status": "ok",
  "model": {"kind": "fs.listing", "data": [{"path": "/home/chris/uploads/SAG-anon",
    "items": [{"name": "sphere.nii.gz", "type": "file", "size": 320}]}]}}]}
}
}
      .o{A .bf{WebSocket} into your live session.}
      .o{Any language can .bf{attach}.}
      .o{Stateless HTTP: .bf{planned}, not shipped.}
    }
    .takeaway{ONE SESSION. ANY SURFACE CAN ATTACH.}
    .source{@fnndsc/menu schemas; exchange derived from them, not captured · mise/guide-session.html}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{intent-raw}
  .title{Without mise}
  .body{
    .h1{Without mise}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> curl cube/api/v1/ --and-then}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 <b>POST</b>  auth-token/                       <i>get a token</i>
 <b>GET</b>   /api/v1/                          <i>discover the file browser</i>
 <b>GET</b>   filebrowser/search/?path=...      <i>find the folder</i>
 <b>GET</b>   folder: children                  <i>subfolders, paged</i>
 <b>GET</b>   folder: files                     <i>files, paged</i>
 <b>GET</b>   folder: link_files                <i>links, paged</i>
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{Six} calls for a small folder.}
      .o{Three lists to .bf{merge} and sort yourself.}
    }
    .takeaway{ONE INTENT, OR A CHAIN OF CALLS.}
    .source{CUBE REST as cumin and salsa call it; folder collections named by link relation}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-session}
  .title{One Session, Many Surfaces}
  .body{
    .h1{One Session, Many Surfaces}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> calypso --berths}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 ┌─────────┐
 │  <b>chell</b>  │──┐
 └─────────┘  │   ┌────────────────────────┐
              ├──<u>▶</u>│        <b>calypso</b>         │        ┌────────┐
 ┌─────────┐  │   │ <i>one login, one session</i> │ ─────<u>▶</u> │  <b>CUBE</b>  │
 │  <b>argus</b>  │──┘   └────────────────────────┘        └────────┘
 └─────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{Work .bf{outlives} its viewer.}
      .o{Type .bf{cd} in the terminal. The browser moves.}
      .o{Like tmux: close it, .bf{reattach} later.}
      .o{The engine .bf{can} sit where the data stays.}
    }
    .takeaway{TWO VIEWS OF ONE SESSION. NEVER TWO COPIES.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise · docs/calypso.adoc}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{mise-door}
  .title{The Door and the Berth}
  .body{
    .h1{The Door and the Berth}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> porter}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
                    ┌─ <b>the door</b> ──┐      ┌─ <b>your berth</b> ───────────┐
 ┌───────────┐      │   <b>porter</b>    │      │  calypso  ·  chell     │      ┌────────┐
 │  browser  │ ───<u>▶</u> │ <i>login page</i>  │ ───<u>▶</u> │  <i>/incoming  /outgoing</i>  │ ───<u>▶</u> │  <b>CUBE</b>  │
 └───────────┘      └─────────────┘      └────────────────────────┘      └────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{porter}: what gdm is to a desktop.}
      .o{No tokens. No URLs to .bf{copy}.}
      .o{.bf{berth}: your own container. Shipping in stages.}
      .o{Your shell is never on .bf{CUBE's} machine.}
    }
    .takeaway{LOG IN ONCE. LAND IN YOUR OWN SESSION.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise · docs/berths.adoc}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{clinic}
  .title{ChRIS in the Clinic}
  .body{
    .h1{ChRIS in the Clinic}
    .h2{Leg-length discrepancy at Boston Children's}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris feed --from=pacs --run=lld}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
            ┌─ <b>one ChRIS feed</b> ──────────────────────────────────────────┐
 ┌──────┐   │ ┌──────┐   ┌───────────┐   ┌─────────┐   ┌──────────────┐ │   ┌──────┐
 │ <b>PACS</b> │──<u>▶</u>│ │ pull │──<u>▶</u>│ <b>LLD model</b> │──<u>▶</u>│ measure │──<u>▶</u>│ DICOM report │ │──<u>▶</u>│ <b>PACS</b> │
 └──────┘   │ └──────┘   └───────────┘   └─────────┘   └──────────────┘ │   └──────┘
            └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                                                            <i>reading room</i>
</pre>}
      .o{A study lands. A .bf{workflow} runs. DICOM goes back.}
      .o{The same .bf{container} as on the bench.}
      .o{.bf{Shadow} trial first. Then a clinical trial.}
      .o{The next model .bf{reuses} the plumbing.}
    }
    .takeaway{SAME CONTRACT, FROM THE BENCH TO THE READING ROOM.}
    .source{Tsai, Samal, Lamonica, Morris, McNeil, Pienaar, Eur Radiol 36:1698-1708 (online Sep 2025), doi:10.1007/s00330-025-12022-0}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{clinic-end}
  .title{Where It Has Run}
  .body{
    .h1{Where It Has Run}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --deployments}
      .o{A .bf{laptop}: miniChRIS in docker-compose.}
      .o{On-prem, wired to clinical .bf{PACS}.}
      .o{Mass Open Cloud: OpenShift, .bf{GPUs}.}
      .o{Two hospitals compare. Neither sees the other's .bf{data}.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE CONTAINER DOESN'T CHANGE. ONLY WHERE IT RUNS.}
    .source{FNNDSC/miniChRIS-docker · FNNDSC/CHRIS_docs · Grant, Red Hat Summit 2019 (ChRIS and multi-party compute)}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{harbor}
  .title{Where ChRIS Sits in HARBOR}
  .body{
    .h1{Where ChRIS Sits in HARBOR}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> harbor td --describe}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 ┌─ <b>Hub TD</b> ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │    marketplace   ·   orchestration   ·   audit   ·   <b>ChRIS</b>     │
 └─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┬──────────────┘
               │ <i>apps and instructions</i>             │
               │              <i>derived results only</i> │
 ╔═ <b>Spoke TD</b> ══<u>▼</u>═══════════════════════════════════<u>▲</u>══════════════╗
 ║  ┌─ <b>ChRIS</b> ──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  ║
 ║  │  ┌─────┐     ┌─────┐     ┌─────┐                         │  ║   <i>raw data</i>
 ║  │  │ app │ ──<u>▶</u> │ app │ ──<u>▶</u> │ app │                         │  ║   <i>stays here</i>
 ║  │  └─────┘     └─────┘     └─────┘                         │  ║
 ║  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤  ║
 ║  │ OpenShift:  namespaces  ·  policy  ·  storage            │  ║
 ║  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  ║
 ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
</pre>}
      .o{Apps .bf{move} to the data.}
      .o{ChRIS in .bf{every} TD, Hub and Spoke.}
      .o{The Hub .bf{dispatches}. The Spoke runs.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE SAME WORKFLOW, UNDER THE SAME CHECKS, IN EVERY TD.}
    .source{HARBOR Task Description Document: System Platform}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{harbor-2}
  .title{The Boundary}
  .body{
    .h1{The Boundary}
    .h2{What ChRIS owns in a Trusted Domain, and what it leaves alone}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --scope}
      .o{.bf{Owns}: apps, pipelines, provenance, run history.}
      .o{.bf{Enforces}: what an app may touch.}
      .o{.bf{Leaves}: clusters, fleet, identity, compliance.}
    }
    .takeaway{ChRIS ISN'T COMPETING WITH OPENSHIFT. IT IS THE LAST MILE ON TOP OF IT.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{harbor-end}
  .title{Ingestion as Apps}
  .body{
    .h1{Ingestion as Apps}
    .h2{Every stage of intake is a ChRIS app}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> harbor ingest --stages}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
         ┌──────────┐   ┌─────────────┐   ┌─────────────┐   ┌───────────┐
  <i>raw</i> ──<u>▶</u>│ <b>validate</b> │──<u>▶</u>│ <b>de-identify</b> │──<u>▶</u>│ <b>deduplicate</b> │──<u>▶</u>│ <b>normalise</b> │──<u>▶</u> <b>promoted</b>
         └─────┬────┘   └─────────────┘   └─────────────┘   └───────────┘
               │ <i>fail</i>
            ┌──<u>▼</u>──────────────┐
            │ reject + report │
            └─────────────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{Validate}: readable DICOM, required fields.}
      .o{.bf{De-identify}: headers, burned-in text, pixels.}
      .o{.bf{Deduplicate}: by image content.}
      .o{.bf{Composed} first. Each app then matures.}
    }
    .takeaway{EACH PARTNER'S STAGE IS A CONTAINER WITH A DIRECTORY ON EITHER SIDE.}
    .source{HARBOR Task Description Document: Data Management}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{roadmap}
  .title{What HARBOR Adds to ChRIS}
  .body{
    .h1{What HARBOR Adds to ChRIS}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --gaps --scale=federation}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 ┌─ <b>Hub</b> ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │         dispatch   ·   telemetry   ·   one record per run          │
 └─────────┬───────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
           │ <i>jobs</i>                              │ <i>status, progress, failure</i>
 ╔═ <b>Spoke</b> ═<u>▼</u>═══════════════════════════════════<u>▲</u>══════════════════════╗
 ║  ┌─────┐   ┌─────┐   ┌─────┐   ┌────────────┐                      ║
 ║  │ app │──<u>▶</u>│ app │──<u>▶</u>│ app │──<u>▶</u>│ <b>provenance</b> │──<u>▶</u> <b>OpenLineage</b>       ║
 ║  └─────┘   └─────┘   └─────┘   └────────────┘                      ║
 ╟────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╢
 ║  OpenShift:  pods  ·  storage  ·  isolation                        ║
 ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{Dispatch}: submit at the Hub, run in a Spoke.}
      .o{.bf{Telemetry}: one record per run.}
      .o{.bf{Recovery}: a Spoke stalls, the run resumes.}
      .o{.bf{Baseline} first. Then measure at scale.}
    }
    .takeaway{THE CONTRACT IS PROVEN. RUNNING IT ACROSS A FEDERATION IS THE FUNDED WORK.}
    .source{HARBOR Task Description Document: App Runtime}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{roadmap-peer}
  .title{One ChRIS to Another}
  .body{
    .h1{One ChRIS to Another}
    .h2{Today, only as a client}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --talk-to=another-chris}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
    <b>Hub</b>                                                <b>Spoke TD</b>
 ┌────────────┐        REST, as a <b>CUBE</b> user        ┌────────────────┐
 │  a client  │ ─────────────────────────────────<u>▶</u> │      <b>CUBE</b>      │
 │   chell,   │                                    ├────────────────┤
 │  a script  │ <u>◀</u>═══════ ws: one session ════════<u>▶</u> │    <b>calypso</b>     │
 └────────────┘  <i>command lines in, envelopes out</i>   └────────────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{REST}: any program, as a CUBE user.}
      .o{.bf{WebSocket}: attach to a session at the Spoke.}
      .o{Either way a .bf{client}. Never a peer.}
    }
    .takeaway{TODAY ONE ChRIS CAN ONLY BE A CLIENT OF ANOTHER.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise · docs/calypso.adoc, packages/menu/src/messages.ts}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{roadmap-peer-2}
  .title{The Gaps Between Them}
  .body{
    .h1{The Gaps Between Them}
    .h2{The wire was built for a person at a prompt}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> diff operator hub}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 ┌──────────┬───────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┐
 │          │<i> today</i>                 │<i> a Hub needs</i>                │
 ├──────────┼───────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┤
 │ <b>identity</b> │ a user's login        │ to act as itself           │
 │ <b>request</b>  │ a command-line string │ a typed, versioned call    │
 │ <b>delivery</b> │ one live session      │ submit once, resume, retry │
 │ <b>egress</b>   │ not yet classified    │ policy at the Spoke's edge │
 └──────────┴───────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{A Hub is not a .bf{person}.}
      .o{It cannot borrow someone's .bf{session}.}
    }
    .takeaway{SHAPED FOR AN OPERATOR. NOT YET FOR A HUB.}
    .source{github.com/HARBOR-Medical-AI/mise · docs/calypso.adoc, docs/intent-kernel.adoc}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{roadmap-peer-3}
  .title{From Client to Peer}
  .body{
    .h1{From Client to Peer}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --peer --plan}
      .o{<pre class="fig">
 ┌─ <b>Hub</b> ────┐                                                ┌─ <b>Spoke</b> ──┐
 │          │ ───── <b>dispatch</b>: a stateless intent call ─────<u>▶</u> │          │
 │          │                                                │          │
 │          │ <u>◀</u>─────── <b>telemetry</b>: the session wire ───────── │          │
 └─────┬────┘                                                └────┬─────┘
       └─────────── <b>agents</b>: the same intents, as tools ───────────┘
</pre>}
      .o{.bf{Funded}: dispatch, recovery, version agreement.}
      .o{.bf{Planned} in mise: a stateless intent API.}
      .o{.bf{Proposed}: the same intents as MCP tools.}
    }
    .takeaway{TODAY A CLIENT. HARBOR FUNDS THE PEER.}
    .source{HARBOR Task Description Document: App Runtime · mise docs/intent-kernel.adoc}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{roadmap-end}
  .title{Governance and Standards}
  .body{
    .h1{Governance and Standards}
    .h2{Making the record legible outside ChRIS}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris --extensions --for=harbor}
      .o{.bf{App policy}: what an app may touch, enforced.}
      .o{.bf{Audit}: every operation logged and versioned.}
      .o{.bf{Lineage}: an OpenLineage-compatible export.}
      .o{.bf{DICOMweb}: QIDO-RS, WADO-RS, STOW-RS.}
    }
    .takeaway{PROVENANCE AN AUDITOR CAN READ WITHOUT LEARNING ChRIS.}
    .source{HARBOR Task Description Document: App Runtime · Services}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{working}
  .title{Working With It}
  .body{
    .h1{Working With It}
    .h2{Bringing a tool into a HARBOR workflow}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> chris plugin --howto}
      .o{Put the tool in a .bf{container}.}
      .o{Flags and two .bf{directories}. No prompts, no GUI.}
      .o{Describe it in a JSON .bf{descriptor}.}
      .o{.bf{Register} it. Now anyone can use it.}
    }
    .takeaway{TRY THE WHOLE STACK ON A LAPTOP FIRST: miniChRIS.}
    .source{ChRIS Plugin Specification · github.com/FNNDSC/miniChRIS-docker · chrisproject.org}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{working-end}
  .title{What We Need to Agree}
  .body{
    .h1{What We Need to Agree}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> harbor --interfaces --open}
      .o{.bf{Stage contracts}: what sits between two stages.}
      .o{.bf{App policy}: what a stage may touch.}
      .o{.bf{Run record}: status, progress, failure.}
      .o{.bf{Lineage mapping}: a run as OpenLineage.}
    }
    .takeaway{AGREE THE DIRECTORIES AND THE EVENTS. THE REST CAN CHANGE UNDERNEATH.}
  }
}

.slide{
  .id{conclusions}
  .title{Conclusions}
  .body{
    .h1{Conclusions}
    .term{
.typewriter{$> exit
> questions?}
      .o{A .bf{workflow runtime}. Provenance is the tree it leaves.}
      .o{Clinical AI at Boston Children's, .bf{today}.}
      .o{In HARBOR: repeatable and auditable in every .bf{TD}.}
      .o{Next: one ChRIS as a .bf{peer} of another.}
    }
  }
}
